{% comment %}
  Secondary labels are gray only on the 2-bit and 4-bit palettes, the ones
  with real gray ink. Elsewhere they stay black: a 1-bit screen dithers gray
  text into speckle (TRMNL's reviewers flag it), and so does every colour
  palette, which has no gray and no prefix to override it with.
{% endcomment %}

{% comment %}
  Reusable blocks for the four layouts. The payload is built by
  apps/web/src/lib/trmnl/payload.ts and is fully formatted there:
  times are already in the owner's zone and language, so nothing here does
  date arithmetic. Liquid computing "time until" would freeze whenever the
  payload is unchanged, because TRMNL skips the redraw.
{% endcomment %}

{% comment %}
  `w--full`: TRMNL's value fitting shrinks the value to its parent's width,
  and in a centred flex column that parent is otherwise exactly as wide as the
  text, so a long winner's name never shrank.
{% endcomment %}
{% template lead %}
<div class="flex flex--col gap--xsmall w--full">
  <span class="title lg:title--large">{{ lead.label }}</span>
  <span class="value {{ size }}" data-value-fit="true">{{ lead.value }}</span>
</div>
{% endtemplate %}

{% comment %}
  Flag, race name, circuit, then round and dates, on three lines in every
  layout. The flag is decoration beside the name: in grayscale Italy, Ireland
  and Mexico are the same three stripes, so it can never be the only thing that
  says which race this is.

  `name_size` is the race name's size on large screens (the full layout has
  room for `lg:title--xlarge`, the halves and quarter wrap it), and
  `detail_size` the circuit and round's, a step below the name. `flag_size`
  sets the flag's height, matched in each layout to the
  height of the three lines beside it (measured on the OG and the X); its width follows the flag's own shape, capped for
  Qatar, whose file's viewBox is 75:18 and stretches to fit.
  Widths over 128px use the named scale (`lg:w--max-48` is 192px): the
  Framework only generates bracketed sizes up to `[128px]`, and a larger one
  silently does nothing, which squeezed every flag on the X into the OG's cap.
  `shrink-0` keeps the shape in a narrow column, where flex shrank the width
  and not the height.

  Nothing is clamped: an ellipsis cut the dates off. The dates never split
  ("1 – 3 May"): their spaces become non-breaking here, because the Framework's
  label is a flex container that swallowed the space before a nested no-wrap
  span, and it has no text no-wrap class.

  The circuit and round are black, not gray: on the X, gray small labels
  were too faint to read at arm's length, and size alone already sets them
  below the name.

  The 1px border frames the flag itself, so white fields (Japan, Monaco,
  Poland) keep an edge against the white screen. Border is not among the
  inline styles TRMNL's Chef linter flags.
{% endcomment %}
{% template race_header %}
<div class="flex flex--row flex--left flex--center-y gap--small">
  {% if race.flag_url %}
  <img class="image image-dither shrink-0 w--auto {{ flag_size }}" style="border: 1px solid #000" src="{{ race.flag_url }}" alt="">
  {% endif %}
  <div class="flex flex--col flex--left gap--none">
    <span class="title {{ name_size }}">{{ race.name }}</span>
    {% if race.circuit %}<span class="label label--small {{ detail_size }}">{{ race.circuit }}</span>{% endif %}
    <span class="label label--small {{ detail_size }}">Round {{ race.round }} · {{ race.dates | replace: " ", "&nbsp;" }}</span>
  </div>
</div>
{% endtemplate %}

{% comment %}
  The weekend timeline. `name` picks the row label: "label" spells it out
  ("Free Practice 1", "Sprint Qualifying") where there is room, "short"
  ("FP1", "SQ") where there is not. Each row carries its own forecast.
{% endcomment %}
{% template schedule %}
<table class="table {{ size }}">
  <tbody>
    {% for row in schedule %}
    <tr>
      <td><span class="title title--small lg:title--base">{{ row[name] }}</span></td>
      <td><span class="label label--small lg:label--base">{{ row.when }}</span></td>
      <td>
        {% if row.weather %}
        <span class="flex flex--row flex--left flex--center-y gap--xsmall">
          <img class="image w--[22px] h--[22px] lg:w--[32px] lg:h--[32px]" src="{{ row.weather.icon }}" alt="">
          <span class="label label--small lg:label--base">{{ row.weather.temp }}{% if row.weather.rain != "" %} {{ row.weather.rain }}{% endif %}</span>
        </span>
        {% endif %}
      </td>
      <td>
        {% if row.state == "done" %}
          <span class="label label--small lg:label--base">{{ row.top3 | join: " " }}</span>
        {% elsif row.next %}
          <span class="label label--small label--filled">Next</span>
        {% elsif row.state == "awaiting" %}
          <span class="label label--small 2bit:label--gray 4bit:label--gray">Awaiting result</span>
        {% endif %}
      </td>
    </tr>
    {% endfor %}
  </tbody>
</table>
{% endtemplate %}


{% comment %}
  `headline_size` is always passed. It is not called `size`: liquidjs, which
  renders the /trmnl page, resolves a missing `size` to 0 where TRMNL's Ruby
  Liquid falls back to a default, so the page and the device disagreed.
{% endcomment %}
{% template news %}
<div class="flex flex--col gap--small" data-overflow="true">
  {% for item in news limit: limit %}
  <div class="item">
    <div class="content">
      <span class="title {{ headline_size }}" data-clamp="2">{{ item.headline }}</span>
    </div>
  </div>
  {% endfor %}
</div>
{% endtemplate %}

{% comment %}
  A session result, up to `limit` rows. `split` lays ten rows out as two
  columns of five, for the full layout, where one column of ten would push
  the QR code off the screen. Both are always passed.
{% endcomment %}
{% template result %}
<div class="flex flex--col gap--small">
  <span class="title title--small lg:title--large">{{ result.label }}</span>
  {% if split and result.rows.size > 5 %}
  <div class="columns">
    <div class="column">{% render "result_rows", rows: result.rows, limit: 5, offset: 0 %}</div>
    <div class="column">{% render "result_rows", rows: result.rows, limit: 5, offset: 5 %}</div>
  </div>
  {% else %}
  {% render "result_rows", rows: result.rows, limit: limit, offset: 0 %}
  {% endif %}
</div>
{% endtemplate %}

{% template result_rows %}
<div class="flex flex--col gap--small">
  {% for row in rows limit: limit offset: offset %}
  <div class="item">
    <div class="meta"><span class="index">{{ row.pos }}</span></div>
    <div class="content">
      <span class="title title--small lg:title--large">{{ row.name }}</span>
    </div>
  </div>
  {% endfor %}
</div>
{% endtemplate %}

{% template grid %}
<div class="flex flex--col gap--small">
  <span class="title title--small lg:title--base">Starting grid</span>
  {% assign half = grid.size | plus: 1 | divided_by: 2 %}
  <div class="columns">
    <div class="column">{% render "grid_rows", rows: grid, limit: half, offset: 0 %}</div>
    <div class="column">{% render "grid_rows", rows: grid, limit: half, offset: half %}</div>
  </div>
</div>
{% endtemplate %}

{% comment %}
  `lg:portrait:table--small`: stacked under the timeline on a portrait X, the
  base row height pushed the back of the grid off the screen.
{% endcomment %}
{% template grid_rows %}
<table class="table table--xsmall lg:table--base lg:portrait:table--small">
  <tbody>
    {% for row in rows limit: limit offset: offset %}
    <tr>
      <td><span class="label label--small">{{ row.pos }}</span></td>
      <td><span class="title title--small">{{ row.code }}</span></td>
      <td><span class="label label--small 2bit:label--gray 4bit:label--gray">{{ row.note }}</span></td>
    </tr>
    {% endfor %}
  </tbody>
</table>
{% endtemplate %}

{% comment %}
  The way from the screen to the site, the same on every layout: a short
  caption over the code. `url` is the race's, or the standings' in the
  off-season. The link is the short /t/ form and carries
  utm_source=trmnl, utm_medium=qr and the screen phase as utm_content, for
  PostHog. 3px modules at error-correction level M: about 0.6mm a module on
  the OG, which a phone reads easily.
{% endcomment %}
{% template qr %}
<div class="flex flex--col flex--center gap--xsmall">
  <span class="label label--small lg:label--base">Read more</span>
  {{ url | qr_code: 3, "m" }}
</div>
{% endtemplate %}

{% comment %}
  The lead session's own forecast under the lead, worded as the race pages
  word it ("Partly cloudy · 27°C", "Rain · 23°C · 60%"). Every layout shows
  it: an icon and a temperature alone read as an orphan, and the timeline rows
  only carry the compact form.
{% endcomment %}
{% template lead_weather %}
{% if weather %}
<span class="flex flex--row flex--center flex--center-y gap--xsmall">
  <img class="image w--[24px] h--[24px] lg:w--[32px] lg:h--[32px]" src="{{ weather.icon }}" alt="">
  <span class="label label--small lg:label--base">{{ weather.text }}</span>
</span>
{% endif %}
{% endtemplate %}

{% comment %}
  The off-season screen: the season just run. `standings.title` is "Formula 1
  2026 Standings" and `standings.detail` "After 23 rounds"; before the
  season ends (only the /trmnl page shows it then) they say so instead.
{% endcomment %}
{% template standings_header %}
<div class="flex flex--col flex--left gap--none">
  <span class="title {{ title_size }}">{{ standings.title }}</span>
  <span class="label label--small {{ detail_size }}">{{ standings.detail }}</span>
</div>
{% endtemplate %}

{% comment %}The champion, as the lead: "2026 champion", then the name.{% endcomment %}
{% template leader %}
<div class="flex flex--col gap--xsmall w--full">
  <span class="title lg:title--large">{{ standings.leader_label }}</span>
  <span class="value {{ value_size }}" data-value-fit="true">{{ standings.drivers.first.name }}</span>
</div>
{% endtemplate %}

{% comment %}
  One championship table, drivers or constructors: position, name, points.
  `label`, `limit`, `offset` and `size` are always passed. An empty label
  leaves the second driver column aligned below the shared heading.
{% endcomment %}
{% template standings_table %}
<div class="flex flex--col gap--xsmall">
  {% if label != "" %}<span class="title title--small lg:title--base">{{ label }}</span>{% endif %}
  <table class="table {{ size }}">
    <tbody>
      {% for row in rows limit: limit offset: offset %}
      <tr>
        <td><span class="label label--small">{{ row.pos }}</span></td>
        <td><span class="title title--small">{{ row.name }}</span></td>
        <td><span class="label label--small">{{ row.points }}</span></td>
      </tr>
      {% endfor %}
    </tbody>
  </table>
</div>
{% endtemplate %}

{% template title_bar %}
<div class="title_bar">
  <img class="image" src="https://grandprixpicks.com/trmnl-icon.svg" alt="">
  <span class="title">GrandPrixPicks.com</span>
</div>
{% endtemplate %}
